        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="what-it-is" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. What a Portable Blender Is, and What It Is Not
          </h2>

          <p>
            A portable blender is a small blade assembly on top of a rechargeable battery and motor, with a jar that usually doubles as your cup. You fill it, press a button, and drink from the same container. That is the entire appeal: no outlet, no counter, no separate glass to wash. For protein shakes after a workout, a smoothie at your desk, or a quick drink at a campsite, a cordless portable blender is genuinely convenient.
          </p>

          <p>
            What it is not is a small version of a kitchen blender. A countertop blender runs on 1,000 watts or more from the wall. A battery powered blender runs on a small lithium-ion pack, and its motor has a fraction of that power. Manufacturers do not always publish motor wattage for their cordless models, and that silence tells you something. The practical result is that a rechargeable blender mixes liquids and soft ingredients well, handles some frozen fruit with enough liquid, and struggles with anything thick, dry or packed with ice.
          </p>

          <p>
            That gap is where most disappointment comes from. People buy a rechargeable blender expecting a frozen smoothie with the texture of a smoothie-shop drink and get a chunky, half-blended cup and a motor that stops and blinks at them. The fix is mostly technique and expectations, which this guide covers, but some buyers would genuinely be happier with a cheap corded blender and, if they camp, a power station to run it.
          </p>

          <p>
            This roundup covers four cordless picks and two corded ones on purpose. The Ninja Blast, Ninja Blast Max, BlendJet 2 and Cuisinart EvolutionX hand blender all run on batteries. The Oster MyBlend and NutriBullet Pro 900 plug in, and they are here because for some readers they are the better answer. If you already carry one of the stations in our <a href="/best-portable-power-station/">best portable power station</a> guide, a corded personal blender is a real option at camp.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="at-a-glance" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. Portable Blenders Compared
          </h2>

          <p>
            The table lines up the six picks on the things that decide whether a portable blender suits you: how it is powered, how much it holds, and what it is realistically good at. Capacities come from manufacturer listings. Where a maker does not publish a figure, we have left it out rather than guess.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Blender</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Power</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Capacity</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Charging</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Best For</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Ninja Blast</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Cordless battery</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">18 oz</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">USB-C</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Everyday smoothies, gym, office</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Ninja Blast Max</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Cordless battery</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">22 oz</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">USB-C</td>
